-- title:
--   Prescribed reduced norms at the split places of an Eichler order
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$, let $R$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ and let $N\in\mathbb N$ be such that `IsEichlerOrder R N` holds, i.e. there are $\mathbb Z$-submodules $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$, each an order that is maximal among orders containing it, with $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ and with the relative index of $R$ in $\Lambda_1$ as additive groups equal to $N$. Let $\varepsilon$ assign to each $w$ in the height-one spectrum of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ an element $\varepsilon_w$ of the completion $\mathbb Q_w$ with $v(\varepsilon_w)=1$, so each $\varepsilon_w$ is a unit of the valuation ring. Then there is a unit $u$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ lying in [`Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer R`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L26) — the stabiliser, for the multiplicative action, of the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in R$ and $\alpha$ a finite adèle all of whose components are integral — with the following property at every place $w$. Suppose it is not the case that every nonzero element of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w$ is a unit. Then for every ring isomorphism $\varphi$ from $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w$ onto $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q_w,a,b]$ (coefficients taken along $\mathbb Q\to\mathbb Q_w$) satisfying $\varphi(z\otimes r)=r\cdot(z$ read coordinatewise in $\mathbb Q_w)$ for all $z$ and $r$, one has $\mathrm{nrd}(\varphi(u_w))=\varepsilon_w$, where $u_w$ is the image of $u$ under evaluation at $w$ of the finite adèles, and $\mathrm{nrd}(x)=x_{\mathrm{re}}^2-ax_{\mathrm{imI}}^2-bx_{\mathrm{imJ}}^2+ab\,x_{\mathrm{imK}}^2$. Nothing is asserted at the places where the completion is a division algebra.
--
--   This is the adelic packaging of the classical local surjectivity of the reduced norm, $\mathrm{nrd}(R_w^\times)=\mathbb Z_w^\times$, for an Eichler order at a finite place where the quaternion algebra splits; the prescribed values are realised simultaneously at all such places by a single unit of the finite idelic stabiliser of the order. It feeds the indefinite-case statement [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.exists_nrd_eq_and_forall_exists_isUnitOf_mul_eq_of_isIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.exists_nrd_eq_and_forall_exists_isUnitOf_mul_eq_of_isIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt), where control of reduced norms of idelic units is used in the construction of quaternionic automorphic data.
